{"kind":"request","text":"NF-10: the device binding on a screen host names the wrong origin. NF-7 run 4 (c2c171d3): join, session and confirmation read all answered 200; the page then threw in deviceSigner (apps/counter/browser/device-key.ts:16) because the binding names https://dap-lending.inguz.workers.dev, from the screen context, while the page runs on https://counter.inguz.space. Builder lane after the NF-9 gate. Ruling: fix where the fact is owned; a platform fix that needs only a deployment beats a Counter 0.6.0 signing.","body":{"conditions":"1. Before code, state with file:line what each side does with binding.origin: what the room or Worker verifies (if anything), what the screen context's origin field means, and what else reads it (API base, links, other apps). 2. Choose the simply correct owner of the fact. Prefer the platform fix if the source allows it: a screen served through a screen host reports the screen host's origin in its context (the origin where the page runs and its key lives), so every installed app (Counter, Lending, Grow) is right without an app change or a new signing. Take the Counter-only change (deviceSigner compares with the context's origin) only if the context origin must stay the service origin; then say why, and say whether Lending or any other installed screen has the same check. 3. One case with a screen host origin different from the service origin that saves and signs, with a named red; the legacy demo path is unchanged. 4. Gate, review, land. Say in the review request whether the hosted fix needs a deployment only, or a 0.6.0 signing and install.","target_head":"f197a89d38426f609bc5c59b0a9babf49edda76c","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}